`dist.ini:9` sets `alien_repo = http://ftp.gnu.org/pub/gnu/gettext`; the `[@Author::GETTY]` bundle turns that into a generated `Build.PL` driven by the deprecated `Alien::Base::ModuleBuild` (see the built tree `Alien-gettext-0.002/Build.PL:2,16,19`: `Dist::Zilla::Plugin::Alien v0.024`, `"protocol" => "http"`, `"Alien::Base::ModuleBuild" => "0.002"`).

On a host without a system gettext this means: the newest tarball listed on ftp.gnu.org is fetched over unencrypted http, with no version pin and no digest, then compiled and installed. The sibling `p5-alien-tinycdb` already moved to an alienfile (its k2, done) and tracks the http/digest follow-up as its k3.

Done when: the dist has an `alienfile` (`alien_build = 1`), the share block fetches from `https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gettext/` (or pins a version plus sha256 digest), a probe decides system vs share, and `CLAUDE.md` / skill `alien-gettext-core` no longer say there is no alienfile.

